Exercise: Say (say)
Difficulty: 6/9

Instructions:
# Instructions

Given a number, your task is to express it in English words exactly as your friend should say it out loud.
Yaʻqūb expects to use numbers from 0 up to 999,999,999,999.

Examples:

- 0 → zero
- 1 → one
- 12 → twelve
- 123 → one hundred twenty-three
- 1,234 → one thousand two hundred thirty-four


Starter file:
```zig
const std = @import("std");
const mem = std.mem;

pub const SayError = error{
    OutOfRange,
};

pub fn say(allocator: mem.Allocator, number: i41) (mem.Allocator.Error || SayError)![]u8 {
    _ = allocator;
    _ = number;
    @compileError("please implement the say function");
}

